legal.dmca2:
Notices may be submitted by:

• rights holders;
• co-holders;
• legally authorized representatives;
• lawyers;
• agents;
• collective management organizations;
• representatives of producers or distributors;
• or other persons who demonstrate sufficient standing.

When the claimant is not the rights holder, they must indicate the capacity in which they are acting.

legal.dmca3:
The notice must clearly identify the holder of the allegedly infringed rights.

The following should be provided, where available:

• full name or company name;
• country of residence or registered office;
• business address;
• email address;
• telephone number;
• identification of the representative;
• and other information necessary to confirm standing.

PixGo may request supporting documentation when there is reasonable doubt about ownership or representation.

legal.dmca4:
The protected work must be identified with sufficient precision.

Depending on the nature of the work, the following may be provided:

• title;
• author;
• producer;
• publisher;
• distributor;
• year of publication;
• registration number;
• ISBN;
• ISRC;
• equivalent identifier;
• description of the work;
• link to an official source;
• or other identifying information.

When the claim covers multiple works, they must be identified individually or through a sufficiently precise description that allows the set covered to be determined.

legal.dmca5:
The location of the content is an essential element for efficient processing of the notice.

The claimant should provide, where available:

• content URL;
• page URL;
• content name;
• video identifier;
• episode identification;
• file identification;
• name of the account that made the content available;
• screenshots;
• or other information that allows the material to be located.

Requests that merely state that a given work appears on the platform, without identifying the specific content, may be considered insufficient.

legal.dmca6:
The notice must clearly explain why the claimant considers the use unlawful.

The description should, whenever possible, indicate:

• what the protected work is;
• what the allegedly infringing content is;
• what use constitutes the alleged infringement;
• what exclusive rights are invoked;
• and why the user would not be authorized to carry out the identified use.

legal.dmca11:
After receiving a notice, PixGo may verify:

• the identity of the claimant;
• the standing presented;
• the identification of the work;
• the location of the content;
• the nature of the claim;
• the existence of known authorization;
• the existence of prior claims;
• any existing counter-notice;
• and other relevant elements.

The review may be carried out manually, technically, or through a combination of both methods.

legal.dmca16:
A user whose content has been removed or whose access has been disabled may, where applicable, submit a counter-notice.

The counter-notice must be sent to:

copyright@pixgo.qzz.io

The counter-notice must clearly identify:

• the user;
• the removed content;
• the previous location of the content;
• the grounds for the dispute;
• contact details;
• and the legally required declarations.

When applicable to a procedure governed by the DMCA, the counter-notice must comply with the specific requirements set out in U.S. law.

legal.dmca17:
After receiving a valid counter-notice, PixGo may reassess the measure previously taken.

The assessment may consider:

• existence of a license;
• authorization from the rights holder;
• ownership of the content;
• misidentification;
• legal exception or limitation;
• withdrawal of the claim;
• court decision;
• or other legally relevant elements.

legal.dmca25:
PixGo may reject or limit the handling of notices that are clearly abusive, fraudulent, or submitted without reasonable grounds.

Notices deliberately intended to, among others, are considered potentially abusive:

• eliminate legitimate content;
• silence criticism;
• interfere with competitors;
• harm third parties;
• obtain a commercial advantage;
• or improperly manipulate the removal system.

